    journal = "Philosophy of the Social Sciences",
    year = "1993",
    volume = "23",
    note = "Asks whether the fall of communism refutes Marxism, rejecting Marxist theories of Stalinism as inadequate and arguing that Stalinism partly rests on non-Marxist elements while Marxism still bears on the verdict. MARX-CENTRALITY: Title (Marxism) and main topic: the truth of Marxism after 1989, rather than Marx's own texts.",
